From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shariq Khalil Ahmed <shariq.ahmed@cohere.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:48:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build libsgx_dcap_quoteverify from Intel's source

The crate links libsgx_dcap_quoteverify, which Intel packages for x86-64
Linux only, so nothing that depends on it builds for macOS or aarch64
Linux.

Fetch Intel's sources with git at pinned commits into OUT_DIR and compile
them, unmodified, into a static library: confidential-computing.tee.dcap
at DCAP_1.27, with its QVL and jwt-cpp submodules, and the public headers
of confidential-computing.sgx.sdk, which DCAP's build takes from an
installed SGX SDK. The source list and include paths follow
QuoteVerification/dcap_quoteverify/linux/Makefile, without the QAL
appraisal engine, which tee_verify_quote does not use, and with the stubs
in place of the generated enclave bridge.

The one portability fix is a define on macOS: se_thread.c names Linux's
__NR_gettid in a function nothing calls.

The bindgen settings are unchanged; the include paths it is given now
point into the fetched sources instead of an installed SDK.
